I did some checking for you and there is a library that comes with X11R6 
called Xtlib.so... You might want to doublecheck that your ldso.conf includes 
/usr/X11R6/lib and make sure that such a file exists (If that's where X is). 
You might also try "man XtCallCallbacks" as there "should" be a man page for 
it. My guess is that the library either is not current enough or your library 
is missing is some way. I found libXt during a search on freshmeat.net, but 
it does come packaged with X.

